<div class="doc">
  <.link navigate={~p"/steer/docs"} class="back">Back to docs</.link>
  <h1>Usage and billing</h1>
  <p class="muted">GET /api/usage, the /usage portal page, and fm-steer usage read the same ledger. Every row is tenant-scoped by the caller's credential.</p>

  <h2>Accounts</h2>
  <p>One row per provider account: provider, label, unit (usd, tokens, credits), allowance per window (monthly, weekly, daily, one_time), used amount, spend priority, source (manual or openrouter), and notes.</p>
  <pre>curl -X POST $PORTAL/api/usage -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;&quot;provider&quot;: &quot;openrouter&quot;, &quot;label&quot;: &quot;captain&quot;,
       &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;usd&quot;, &quot;allowance&quot;: 100, &quot;window&quot;: &quot;monthly&quot;,
       &quot;spend_priority&quot;: 10&#125;'</pre>
  <p>Agents post readings with the <code>record_usage</code> MCP tool or <code>POST /api/usage</code>. Humans add accounts on the /usage page.</p>

  <h2>Remaining, status, runway</h2>
  <p>Remaining is allowance minus used. Status is <code>ok</code> below 75 percent, <code>low</code> above it, <code>exhausted</code> at or past the cap, and <code>unknown</code> when no allowance is set. Unknown allowances stay null through the API, the CLI, and the UI. Nothing is guessed.</p>
  <p>Runway (days until the allowance runs out) comes from snapshot burn rate: at least two samples spanning a day with rising usage. Without that history the API reports <code>runway_days: null</code>.</p>

  <h2>Spend priority</h2>
  <p>Lower numbers burn first. The usage list already arrives in spend order.</p>

  <h2>Sync</h2>
  <p><code>POST /api/usage/sync</code>, <code>fm-steer usage --sync</code>, or the portal Sync button refreshes every syncable account and appends a snapshot per success. Provider tokens live in server-side env vars only.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code></td><td>Syncs OpenRouter key usage. A missing limit keeps any manual allowance.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>AA_API_KEY</code></td><td>Routing intel only. Artificial Analysis sells benchmarks, not spend.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Providers without a live sync report <code>synced: false</code> with the reason and keep their manual readings.</p>
</div>
